  "macroTheme": "Historic AI/semis rout on Democratic midterm sweep fears of data-centre restrictions; oil crashes 14% on Iran ceasefire hopes; gold surges 3% as hedge bid; October payrolls crush forecasts pushing December Fed hike to 77-80%; BoE hikes to 4.00%; VIX at 25.64 signalling sustained volatility regime shift.",
  "macroOverview": "A violent risk-off rotation defined the week ending 06 November. The S&P 500 fell 2.2% but 10 of 11 sectors were positive — the signature of narrow AI/semis concentration dragging benchmarks down. NAS100 suffered its worst day since March 2020 (-6.36%) on Thursday 05 Nov. The semiconductor index crashed 12.25%, its second-biggest drop on record. NVDA -7.6%, AVGO -8.9%, TSLA -11.3% on the week. Oil fell 14% (WTI $89.93, Brent sub-$100) as Democratic Congress raised hopes of ending the US-Iran war. Gold +3.0% on hedge bid despite ceasefire narrative. NFP +165K vs ~59K expected, unemployment 4.1%, wages +0.4% MoM, prior months revised up +84K. December Fed hike odds surged to 77-80%. BoE hiked to 4.00%, RBA and Riksbank also tightened. US30 held 200DMA (50,676) — healthiest of the four major indices.",
